--- body ---

## Context

`bin/idh` exists (`adapters/perch.py`, 512 lines, ticket 0802) with `install`,
`uninstall`, `status`, `relocate` and `check` — but only for skill discovery.
It is not on PATH, not documented in the README, and called by path from two
scripts. Every other lifecycle job has its own entry point:

| Job | Today |
|---|---|
| Skills visible to each runtime | `idh install/uninstall/status` |
| Hooks, settings, config links | `adapters/install-wirings.sh` |
| Pre-launch link check | `scripts/validate-projections.py` (0983) |
| `~/.bashrc` loader block | copied by hand from `scripts/bashrc-loader.sh` |
| Timers | `bin/install-cron`, `scripts/install-mammoth-audit-timer.sh`, `claude-refresh` unit |
| Checkout update | `scripts/sync-local-main.sh`, `claude-harness-pull` |
| Relocation | none yet (0985/0986) |

`install-wirings.sh` and `adapters/projections.json` keep two separate lists of
links, which can drift.

## Decision (author, 2026-09-29)

Three layers, each with one job:

1. **The author, managing a machine** — `idh install | check | status | sync | relocate`.
   Installed by `~/.idh/bin/idh install`, which also links itself into
   `~/.local/bin/idh`. On a new host: clone, then that one command.
2. **The runtimes (hooks, skills, gates)** — keep calling scripts by direct path
   under `~/.idh/scripts/`. Not routed through `idh`: that would add a single
   point of failure and startup cost to every hook.
3. **The rescue path** — the refusing stubs in the `~/.bashrc` loader block and
   the printed `ln -sfn` repairs. Must work when `~/.idh` itself is broken, so it
   never depends on `idh`.

Optional: git-style dispatch (`idh foo` runs `scripts/idh-foo`) for occasional
manual scripts; author convenience only.

## Constraints

- A merge, not a new layer (harness cool-down): each old entry point is deleted as
  its job moves into `idh`. If the first pass does not shrink the total, stop and
  report.
- `projections.json` is the one list: `idh install` creates exactly what `idh check`
  verifies.
- Codex hooks: an untrusted or changed definition silently runs no guard; any
  change to `adapters/codex/hooks.json` needs a `/hooks` re-trust and a fresh
  `codex exec` block probe in the same step.
- Read what the existing `idh relocate` does before extending it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `~/.idh/bin/idh install` on a disposable HOME installs skills, wirings, the loader block and timers from `projections.json`, and links `~/.local/bin/idh`; `idh check` passes right after (positive control), and fails with a named culprit after one planted broken link (negative control)
- [ ] `install-wirings.sh`, the timer installer and the manual loader copy are removed or reduced to a one-line call to `idh`; source growth is limited to safety the deleted scripts lacked (marker-bounded, byte-verified bashrc splice; refusal to overwrite real files or foreign links; no execution of manifest text), measured and stated in the PR (`bin/install-cron` dropped from scope by the 2026-09-29 raid Imagine pass: it installs the `bin/snapshot` telemetry cron, has no callers, and is not part of harness install)
- [ ] `idh sync` fast-forwards the checkout and, when it cannot, names the blocking files (the padme case of 2026-09-29)
- [ ] `idh status` reports installed vs declared and distance to origin
- [ ] README installation section is the two-command bootstrap
- [ ] Hooks and skills still call scripts by path; no hook routes through `idh`
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Imagine annotation (raid 2026-09-29)

Not monster-shaped: about 136 lines absorbed (`adapters/install-wirings.sh` 120,
`scripts/install-mammoth-audit-timer.sh` 16); the doc and test propagation is the
ordinary multiplier, not a dependency chain.

Simplest path:
1. Give `scripts/bashrc-loader.sh` an explicit END marker; `idh install` splices
   between the markers and proves the lines outside are byte-identical to a backup
   (see the 2026-09-29 log note on padme).
2. `idh install` creates each `projections.json` entry from its structured fields
   (`mkdir -p` + `os.symlink`), reusing `validate-projections.py`'s read side.
3. `idh check` wraps `scripts/validate-projections.py`, all runtimes by default.
4. `idh sync` wraps `scripts/sync-local-main.sh` unchanged; `idh status` is new
   but small (installed vs declared, distance to origin).
5. Delete `install-wirings.sh` and the timer installer once absorbed.

Out of scope, stated so it cannot creep in: extending `idh relocate` (today it
retargets skill links only; the full move is 0985/0986); the `idh foo` dispatch;
`bin/install-cron`.

Constraints from the Blind-Spot pass:
- **Never execute manifest text.** The repair strings contain the free-form
  `installer` field, and the checkout auto-pulls from origin. `idh install` acts
  on structured fields only, never `sh -c` on a string.
- **The `~/.claude` manifest entry is provisional until 0984 reports.** If native
  memory is not followed through links, 0985 re-derives it; 0987 must not bake in
  today's meaning.
- **Rewrite the `installer` fields** that name `install-wirings.sh` in the same
  commit that deletes it, so no refusal prints a dead repair.
- **Systemd units:** on doudou, `claude-telemetry-prune.service` (hardcodes
  `%h/.claude/telemetry`) and `claude-refresh.timer` name `.claude`; padme has
  none; no crontab on either host. The plan states which units `idh install`
  owns; ones it does not own are listed for 0985/0986.
- **padme runs Python 3.12.3** (doudou 3.14.4); `validate-projections.py` and
  `adapters/perch.py` byte-compile there. New code stays 3.12-compatible, with a
  test run under 3.12 if available.

## Actions (raid plan 2026-09-29)

Decisions: new `adapters/lifecycle.py` (stdlib, Python 3.12-compatible) reusing
`scripts/validate-projections.py` via importlib; `perch.py` is not grown, `bin/idh`
routes `install` (no args), `check [runtime]`, `status`, `sync` to lifecycle and
falls back to perch for `install skill X` and the rest. Units owned: only
`idh-mammoth-audit.{service,timer}`, the one pair versioned in `systemd/`;
`claude-refresh` and `claude-telemetry-prune` live only in `~/.config/systemd/user`
(telemetry-prune hardcodes `%h/.claude/telemetry`) and are listed for 0985/0986.
Links come from `path`/`target` only; `installer` is display text, never executed.

Commits, one change each:
1. Begin/end markers in `scripts/bashrc-loader.sh`; update the README copy step,
   the `on-start.sh` reminder and the marker assertions in
   `tests/test_projection_validator.py`, `tests/test_idh_root_literals.py`.
2. `lifecycle.py` install/check (red test first): per entry, skip if correct,
   create if absent, refuse and name a real file or foreign link (continue, exit
   non-zero); optional entries only when the target exists; link
   `~/.local/bin/idh`. `check` calls `check_entry` per runtime, all by default.
   Nothing special-cases `~/.claude`.
3. Bashrc block: back up to `~/.bashrc.idh-bak`, splice between the markers,
   assert the bytes outside equal the backup's (restore and exit 1 on mismatch);
   refuse a legacy start marker with no end marker and print the manual step;
   append when no block; a rerun is a no-op. Tests include trailing user lines
   surviving (the padme alias case).
4. Timers: fold the mammoth installer into lifecycle (`systemctl` by argv list;
   "timers skipped" when absent); repoint `tests/test_mammoth_audit.py`; delete
   `scripts/install-mammoth-audit-timer.sh`; README.
5. Wirings: rewrite the two `installer` fields to `idh install`; repoint
   `tests/test_adapter_deployment.py`, `tests/test_idh_pointer_hooks.py` and the
   validator assertion; delete `adapters/install-wirings.sh`; fix
   `docs/adapter-operations.md`. Keep wiring uninstall only if something beyond
   tests needs it.
   **Line-budget gate here:** `git diff --stat main` over source files (not tests
   or docs). If the net is not down, stop and report, as the constraint says.
6. `sync` runs `scripts/sync-local-main.sh` unchanged, relays its output (it names
   blocking files) and exits non-zero if still behind (`rev-list --count`);
   `status` prints `ok|MISSING|DANGLING|FOREIGN path -> target` per entry, timer
   state, ahead/behind origin, `declared N, ok M`, exit 1 if anything is broken.
7. README install section: the two commands. No `hooks.json` change, so no
   Codex re-trust.
8. `make check`; py_compile under 3.12 if available (absent on doudou; say so).

## First test (raid plan)

`tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py::test_install_then_check_round_trip_and_planted_break`:
disposable HOME in `tmp_path`, PATH `tmp/bin:/usr/bin:/bin` with a `systemctl`
stub logging argv. Asserts: install exits 0; `check` exits 0 (positive control);
every required entry is a symlink resolving to its declared target (the expected
set comes from the manifest, not from what install created); `~/.local/bin/idh`
resolves to `bin/idh`; the stub logged `--user enable --now idh-mammoth-audit.timer`;
retargeting `~/.codex/hooks.json` to `/nonexistent` makes `check` exit 1 naming
exactly that path, one culprit line. Avoid: comparing install output with check
output, or asserting only "block present" for the splice.

## Dependencies (raid plan)

Steps 1-2 before 3-6; 5 needs 2. Nothing waits on 0984: `~/.claude` stays one
generic manifest row. Rebase at each gate (0985/0986 touch `projections.json`).

## Line budget (raid plan)

Removed: `install-wirings.sh` 120 + `install-mammoth-audit-timer.sh` 16 = 136.
Estimated `lifecycle.py` about 160, so the net is likely NOT down on source alone
(about 40% odds of a drop); offsets are dropping wiring uninstall/status (~45) and
a shorter deployment test. The step-5 gate decides.
